- Technical Details
    - Tech Stack:
        - Python 3.11+ (developed on 3.12)
        - numpy, scipy, statsmodels, pandas, matplotlib, pyarrow
        - pymc (Bayesian engine), arviz (posterior diagnostics)
        - pytest, jupyter, nbconvert, ipykernel for testing and notebooks
        - loglog for documentation source -> markdown rendering
    - Key Files:
        - `pyproject.toml` -- declares the expkit package and its deps
        - `expkit/` -- the library (sim, inference, plot, io for Phase 1; rest scaffolded)
        - `chapters/01-the-coin/` -- the first complete chapter; reference shape for all others
        - `chapters/NN-*/chapter.log` -- stubs for chapters 2-19 with carried question + inquiry-loop sketch
        - `data/manifest.yaml` -- cross-cutting reproducibility manifest
        - `scripts/regenerate_all.py` -- regenerate every chapter's data from seeds
        - `scripts/render_chapters.py` -- loglog -> markdown for every chapter.log
    - Architecture Notes:
        - Each chapter is self-contained: narrative, code, images, data, regeneration script all live in one folder
        - `expkit` is the cross-chapter library; chapters import from it rather than duplicate logic
        - Both frequentist and Bayesian (PyMC) lenses appear in every chapter
        - All randomness is seeded; sha256 of every artifact is recorded in `data/manifest.yaml`

